        "type": "text",
        "text": "Official statistics for Iceland from the PX-Web database of Statistics Iceland (Hagstofa Íslands). This server is not affiliated with or endorsed by Statistics Iceland.\n\nTo answer a question with data:\n1. Call `search_tables` with short topic keywords in English (\"en\") or Icelandic (\"is\"). The English and Icelandic table lists are not the same, so use a table id only in the language that returned it. You can also search for a table number such as MAN00101 if no other table has the same number.\n2. Call `get_table_metadata` on the best table to see its variables and value codes. Use `valueFilter` to find a municipality or industry by name.\n3. Call `query_table` with only the values you need. Use `latest` for recent periods.\n\nAlways cite the source line that each result ends with. If you change the data or calculate new figures, say so, for example \"Statistics Iceland and own calculations\"."
      }
    ],
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hver eru meðallaun á Íslandi?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "tools": [
      {
        "name": "search_tables",
        "description": "Find tables by keywords in their titles. Returns table ids, titles and publish dates, best match first. Search with short topic words, for example \"unemployment municipalities\", not full questions.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
          "properties": {
            "query": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 2,
              "description": "Keywords to search for."
            },
            "lang": {
              "description": "Language of titles. Default \"en\".",
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "en",
                "is"
              ]
            },
            "limit": {
              "description": "Maximum results. Default 10.",
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "maximum": 50
            },
            "includeArchived": {
              "description": "Also list discontinued tables, for older periods. Default false.",
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "query"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "get_table_metadata",
        "description": "List the variables of a table and their value codes. Call this before query_table. Long value lists are shortened; use valueFilter to find specific values, for example a municipality name.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
          "properties": {
            "tableId": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "description": "Table id exactly as search_tables returns it."
            },
            "lang": {
              "description": "Language of labels. Default \"en\".",
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "en",
                "is"
              ]
            },
            "valueFilter": {
              "description": "Show only values whose label contains this text, for example \"Ljubljana\".",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "tableId"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "query_table",
        "description": "Get data from a table as CSV with readable labels. For each variable, give value codes from get_table_metadata, or \"latest\" for the most recent N periods. Results above 5000 cells, or too large for the context, are refused with advice on how to narrow the query.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
          "properties": {
            "tableId": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "description": "Table id exactly as search_tables returns it."
            },
            "lang": {
              "description": "Language of labels. Default \"en\".",
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "en",
                "is"
              ]
            },
            "selections": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "code": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Variable code from get_table_metadata."
                  },
                  "values": {
                    "description": "Value codes to include.",
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  },
                  "latest": {
                    "description": "Include only the last N values. Use it for time variables, for example the latest 4 quarters.",
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "maximum": 9007199254740991
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "code"
                ]
              },
              "description": "One entry per variable to filter. Leave out variables you do not need."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "tableId",
            "selections"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
